This report summarizes the outcomes of the CVPR 2022 AQTC contest, focusing on 'Love is in the Air', an accessory quarlized tail challenge. The main aim of this contest was to identify an image classification model that could effectively, efficiently, and accurately classify images impacted by various forms of noise. The reporting guidelines for this contest were designed to be comprehensive, covering seven key areas, and the winning entries from both the track and challenge are presented in detail. The "Love is in the Air" dataset is also made accessible for public use through the AQTC repository. The code can be accessed via the AQTC repository, referencing repository number 30695. 

